Fixed: /doctor's API row now says <host> rejected the API key (HTTP 400) for a bad Google or xAI key. Before, it said "answered with an error (HTTP 400)" and printed the vendor's error text. The fix is in commit b99d435, and fmt, clippy (-D warnings) and the full cargo test all pass afterwards.

What changed
• One shared check. The three bad-key phrases (api_key_invalid, api key not valid, incorrect api key) now live in one function, body_says_key_rejected, in src/doctor_api.rs. The run's error diagnosis (diagnose_api_error_for) calls it instead of its own copy of the three lines, and /doctor calls it too, so they can't drift apart. A plain 400 or INVALID_ARGUMENT doesn't count as a bad key, because those also cover bad fields.
• File size. src/prompt_retry.rs went from 2796 to 2793 lines, under its 2800 cap.
• Tests. A local stub returns the real Google and xAI bad-key replies recorded on Day 254, through yoagent's actual google and xai providers. I reused the existing constants (now pub(crate)) rather than retyping them. Each test checks the row's whole text. A near-miss test checks that a Google 400 about a bad max_output_tokens still says "answered with an error". The 13 existing bad-key diagnosis tests passed without changes.
• Recall check. With the new check disabled, the Google and xAI tests failed and printed the old "answered with an error" text. With it restored, all 15 /doctor API tests pass. I posted this result on #1243 before running the full checks.
• Docs. common-issues.md no longer says these keys show up as "answered with an error", which was the "Limits" claim from the #1242 commit. commands.md now lists the Google/xAI 400 under "rejected the API key".

The commit says Fixes #1243, so the issue closes when this is pushed.
